      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 908,
        "height": 344,
        "content": "## 1. Work out the target month\nOne Code node turns today's date into the three strings everything else needs: the tab name, the folder name and the archive name."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "8da00bb8-9b0f-443e-8557-8f9ab7996c05",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Section 2",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        2176,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 2028,
        "height": 720,
        "content": "## 2. Find or create the folder, and skip if done\nThe month folder is created when it does not exist. If an archive for that month is already in it, the run stops here, so re-running is always safe."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "56e5ff85-ca27-4f34-a371-605d1122b380",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Section 3",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        4256,
        368
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1188,
        "height": 600,
        "content": "## 3. Locate last month's tab\nThe tab list is flattened and searched. If the tab is missing you get an email listing the tabs that do exist, instead of a silent empty run."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "222d8e69-3b7b-4248-8119-63247ecfa0c4",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Section 4",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        5504,
        256
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1188,
        "height": 344,
        "content": "## 4. Build the archive\nA spreadsheet is created through the Sheets API and moved into the folder, no Apps Script needed. The tab is copied in, then one batch call renames it, freezes and bolds the header, sizes the columns and deletes the empty default sheet."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "57efae7a-13be-4d75-8c2e-02ccd9bd7c4c",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Section 5",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        6736,
        96
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "color": 7,
        "width": 1188,
        "height": 504,
        "content": "## 5. Optionally clean up, then report\nWith the config flag on, last month's tab is removed from the working sheet once the archive exists. Either way you get an email with the row count and a link."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "90feb6c0-e65d-40d5-9b24-204503bbc31d",
      "name": "Sticky Note - Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        0,
        0
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 633,
        "content": "# Archive last month's invoice tab into a dated Drive folder\n\nOn the first of every month this lifts last month's tab out of your working invoice spreadsheet, files a formatted copy inside that month's Drive folder, and emails you a link. The working sheet stops growing forever and your accountant gets one clean file per month, next to the invoices themselves.\n\n### How it works\n1. A Code node works out last month once and hands the tab, folder and archive names to every node after it.\n2. Drive is searched for the month folder, for example 2026-03, and it is created if missing.\n3. The folder is checked for an archive of that month. If one exists the run stops, so re-running never duplicates.\n4. The tab list is searched for last month. If it is missing you get an email listing the tabs that do exist.\n5. A new spreadsheet is created through the Sheets API and moved into the folder, so no Apps Script is needed.\n6. The tab is copied in, then one batch call renames it, freezes and bolds the header, sizes columns and deletes the empty default sheet.\n7. With the config flag on, last month's tab is deleted from the working sheet, but only after the archive exists. You then get a summary email with a link.\n\n### Setup\n1. Connect your Google account on the Sheets API nodes, Drive on the folder nodes, and Gmail.\n2. Open Set config and add your spreadsheet ID, the parent folder holding your month folders, email and timezone.\n3. Tabs must be named like March 2026 and month folders like 2026-03.\n4. Leave removeTabAfterArchiving off until you trust the archive.\n\n### Customization\nChange archiveSuffix for something other than Invoices in the file name."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    }
  ],
